  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Viasat's federal business totaled $334M in obligations in FY2026 to date. Viasat won 124 awards so far, with an average award size of $2.7M, and obligations are up 22.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $213M, followed by the General Services Administration with $119M. The company sees its largest market in Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $190M, with Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $75M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $29.5M. Viasat's fiscal-year obligations have varied: FY21 $484M, FY22 $561M, FY23 $527M, FY24 $341M, FY25 $273M, and FY26 $334M. These figures are contract obligations except where noted as total contract values in award tables. This snapshot covers fiscal year to date and represents partial current-year totals. Use these figures to compare buyers, market focus, and recent momentum in Viasat's federal contracting profile.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Viasat's federal business changed over the last five fiscal years?",
        "body": "Viasat's fiscal-year obligations rose from FY25 to FY26, going from $273M to $334M. Viasat's highest obligations in the last six fiscal years were FY22 at $561M and FY23 at $527M. Viasat's obligations in FY24 were $341M, and FY21 was $484M. These year-by-year figures show the scale and variability of recent federal contracting with Viasat."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets drive Viasat's federal dollars?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the top buyer, obligating $213M, followed by the General Services Administration with $119M. Viasat's largest market is Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $190M, with Guided Missile and Space Vehicle Manufacturing at $75M and Radio and Television Broadcasting and Wireless Communications Equipment Manufacturing at $29.5M. Other notable markets include Satellite Telecommunications at $15.5M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $12.6M."
      }
    ]
  },
